{
 "total": 68.587,
 "scenes": [
  {
   "v": "hook_fire",
   "start": 0.0,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "The oldest proof of people making fire was found in England.",
     "start": 0.6,
     "end": 3.837
    },
    {
     "text": "And it's about four hundred thousand years old.",
     "start": 4.157,
     "end": 6.458
    }
   ],
   "end": 6.828
  },
  {
   "v": "hook_q",
   "start": 6.828,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "So how did cavemen make fire?",
     "start": 7.128,
     "end": 8.795
    }
   ],
   "end": 9.165
  },
  {
   "v": "meet_moss",
   "start": 9.165,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Meet Moss. He's rubbing sticks. Nothing.",
     "start": 9.465,
     "end": 11.798
    }
   ],
   "end": 12.168
  },
  {
   "v": "wonderwerk",
   "start": 12.168,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Surprise one: using fire is even older.",
     "start": 12.468,
     "end": 15.211
    },
    {
     "text": "In Wonderwerk Cave, South Africa, there's ash and burnt bone from about a million years ago.",
     "start": 15.531,
     "end": 20.65
    }
   ],
   "end": 21.02
  },
  {
   "v": "use_vs_make",
   "start": 21.02,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "But using fire isn't making it.",
     "start": 21.32,
     "end": 23.094
    },
    {
     "text": "Maybe they grabbed flames from wildfires.",
     "start": 23.414,
     "end": 25.8
    }
   ],
   "end": 26.17
  },
  {
   "v": "barnham",
   "start": 26.17,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Surprise two: at Barnham, people lit fires in one spot, again and again.",
     "start": 26.47,
     "end": 30.787
    },
    {
     "text": "It got hotter than seven hundred degrees.",
     "start": 31.107,
     "end": 33.211
    }
   ],
   "end": 33.581
  },
  {
   "v": "pyrite",
   "start": 33.581,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Surprise three: two little pieces of a rock called pyrite.",
     "start": 33.881,
     "end": 37.192
    },
    {
     "text": "Strike it with flint, and you get sparks.",
     "start": 37.512,
     "end": 39.594
    }
   ],
   "end": 39.964
  },
  {
   "v": "brought",
   "start": 39.964,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Pyrite isn't found naturally there.",
     "start": 40.264,
     "end": 42.195
    },
    {
     "text": "So someone probably brought it, to start fires.",
     "start": 42.515,
     "end": 45.04
    }
   ],
   "end": 45.41
  },
  {
   "v": "who",
   "start": 45.41,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Who? Experts think early Neanderthals.",
     "start": 45.71,
     "end": 48.058
    }
   ],
   "end": 48.428
  },
  {
   "v": "handaxes",
   "start": 48.428,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Surprise four: Neanderthals in France left clues too.",
     "start": 48.728,
     "end": 51.787
    },
    {
     "text": "Scratches on their hand axes suggest striking pyrite for sparks.",
     "start": 52.107,
     "end": 55.826
    }
   ],
   "end": 56.196
  },
  {
   "v": "sticks",
   "start": 56.196,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Rubbing sticks? Maybe. But wood rots, so there's no proof that old.",
     "start": 56.496,
     "end": 60.332
    }
   ],
   "end": 60.702
  },
  {
   "v": "moss_spark",
   "start": 60.702,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Moss tried pyrite. A spark! Right onto his hair.",
     "start": 61.002,
     "end": 63.862
    }
   ],
   "end": 64.232
  },
  {
   "v": "follow",
   "start": 64.232,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Follow for more Stone Age Stories.",
     "start": 64.532,
     "end": 66.417
    }
   ],
   "end": 68.587
  }
 ]
}